Thought: To determine the number of carbonyl groups in the compound, I should first analyze the IR spectra, as carbonyl groups typically show a strong absorption band around 1700 cm^-1. This will help identify the presence of carbonyl groups. If needed, I can further confirm using 13C NMR spectra, as carbonyl carbons have characteristic chemical shifts. However, I'll start with the IR spectra to minimize costs.
Action: ir_spectra
